  "_about": [
    "The four canonical levels are a US high-school ladder, inherited from the TESS",
    "layer. They carry UK qualifications better than expected: a British first degree",
    "and an American bachelor's land together, GCSEs and a high school diploma land",
    "together. That makes the UK and US layers comparable at no cost, which is the",
    "whole point of the project and was not guaranteed.",
    "",
    "Seven UK studies share one YouGov 18-level scheme covering 83% of UK rows, so",
    "the work was mapping three outliers into it rather than inventing a new ladder.",
    "SocSci210 itself harmonises nothing \u2014 sampling six of its studies returns one",
    "vocabulary because nearly every TESS study used the same US panel vendor. Our",
    "corpus is the same shape, and the same strategy applies: translate the minority.",
    "",
    "A fifth canonical value exists for LOGVPZ alone. Read its note below before",
    "adding anything else to the canonical list."
  ]
